<h2><a id="Presentació" name="Presentació"></a>Presentation and options</h2>

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> <br/>
  
<p>For more information on the specifications of the NetCDF format connect to: <a href="https://www.unidata.ucar.edu/software/netcdf/">https://www.unidata.ucar.edu/software/netcdf/</a></p>

<p>In this first version not all the different possibilities provided by the NetCDF format are implemented. Before importing into MiraMon it is necessary to check that the data comply with a number of restrictions. These should be progressively eliminated as new versions of MiraMon are released should users require:</p>

<ul>
  <li>The data must correspond to point observations or to a time series format. If they correspond to a raster format or a <i>grid</i> they will have to be imported as points and then re-rasterised using the <a href="TiraVEC.htm">TiraVEC</a> application. </li>

  <li>The original reference system must be latitude/longitude. By default the datum is taken as ED50, and it is possible to reproject to any other reference system supported by MiraMon. Bear in mind that if the datum is not correctly identified the reprojection may contain displacements.</li>

  <li>The original format should have three spatial dimensions and these must be identified as: <i>lon</i> for the longitude, <i>lat</i> for the latitude and <i>alt</i> for the altitude. This means that the resultant MiraMon file is 3 dimensional.</li>
	
</ul>
  
<p>If you have a NetCDF file that does not conform to these conditions you may contact <a href="mailto:contacte@miramon.uab.cat">contacte@miramon.uab.cat</a> to try to correctly identify your format and to find solutions to allow its import to MiraMon.</p>

<p>All the numerical and alphanumeric fields identified in the original format are gathered into the database of the points file. If there exist time series for these fields, that is, if there exist for the same location values of a variable at different points in time, a multiple record will be created which contains the different values as different records for the same graphical entity.</p>

